---
/** UK privacy notice (UK GDPR, Data Protection Act 2018, PECR), Glasgow Phase 2.
 *  A separate file per country by owner decision (2026-10-22): the US page stays untouched.
 *  Written to describe only what the site does TODAY: no analytics, no advertising, no accounts.
 *  Not legal advice -- the owner reviews this before the site is made indexable. */
import { siteConfig } from '../../../lib/site-config';
---
<article class="prose">
  <h1>Privacy</h1>
  <p><em>Last updated October 2026.</em></p>

  <p>{siteConfig.siteName} is a simple website with no user accounts or logins. This page explains what
  personal data we handle, why, and what your rights are under UK data protection law (the UK GDPR, the Data
  Protection Act 2018 and the Privacy and Electronic Communications Regulations).</p>

  <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
  <p>{siteConfig.siteName} is run by Claudio Fransson, an individual based in Sweden (see <a href="/about/">about</a>).
  Claudio Fransson is the data controller: the controller decides how the data described here is used, and is the contact for anything on this page:
  <a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.removalEmail}`}>{siteConfig.removalEmail}</a>.</p>

  <h2>What we collect, and why</h2>
  <p><strong>Server logs.</strong> Our hosting provider, Cloudflare, keeps standard logs (such as IP address and
  browser type) so the site can be delivered securely and reliably. Our lawful basis is legitimate interests:
  keeping the site working and protecting it from abuse. See
  <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" rel="noopener">Cloudflare's privacy policy</a>.</p>
  <p><strong>If you email us or use the contact form.</strong> We use your email address and message only to
  reply to you. We do not add you to a mailing list or share your details. Our lawful basis is legitimate
  interests (answering you); we keep correspondence only as long as we need it to deal with your request.</p>
  <p><strong>Choices stored in your browser.</strong> Your browser's local storage may hold preferences such as
  light or dark mode. These stay on your device and are not sent to us.</p>

  <h2>Analytics and advertising</h2>
  <p>At the moment this site uses no analytics and shows no advertising, and it sets no analytics or
  advertising cookies. If that ever changes, we will ask for your consent <em>before</em> anything is set, make
  refusing as easy as accepting, and update this page and the <a href="/cookies/">cookies page</a> first.</p>

  <h2>Where data goes</h2>
  <p>Our hosting and email providers may process data outside the UK, including in the United States. Where they
  do, they rely on the safeguards UK law requires, such as the UK's approved transfer mechanisms.</p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>You can ask us to give you a copy of the personal data we hold about you, correct it, erase it, restrict how
  we use it, or stop using it for legitimate interests, and you can ask for it in a portable format. Email
  <a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.removalEmail}`}>{siteConfig.removalEmail}</a> and we will reply within one month.</p>
  <p>If you are unhappy with how we handle your data, you have the right to complain to the Information
  Commissioner's Office: <a href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/" rel="noopener">ico.org.uk</a>. We would
  appreciate the chance to put things right first.</p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>If what we collect changes beyond what is described here, this page and the
  <a href="/cookies/">cookies page</a> will be updated first.</p>

  <p>Questions? <a href="/contact/">Contact us</a>.</p>
</article>

<style>
.prose { max-width: 36rem; }
.prose h2 { margin-top: 2rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
.prose p { margin: 0 0 1rem; }
</style>
